{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774194394,"nonce":"B8pn+q3JDIYHRs4MKkKGjsr/f0Y=","title":"Browser context injection: extension for element selection and cross-references","message":"A Chrome/Firefox extension that lets users select DOM elements and capture structured context for agent consumption.\n\n**Motivation**: When doing web app development with agents, precisely describing UI elements is difficult (\"the little thingy to the right of the blah\"). Users need a way to point at an element and generate a portable reference that carries implicit context.\n\n**Proposed flow**:\n1. Extension activates element picker overlay (Shadow DOM, like DevTools inspect)\n2. User clicks element — Side Panel shows confirmation with title/note input\n3. Extension captures: CSS selector, XPath, accessibility tree (ARIA label/role), React/Vue component name + props, surrounding HTML (3 levels), key computed styles, element screenshot (captureVisibleTab + canvas crop), source file reference (via element-source library when available)\n4. Sends to Mandible API: POST /api/browser-snippets\n5. Stored in browser_snippets table (new migration, modeled on webhook_events pattern)\n6. Copies `browser:\u003c8-char-hash\u003e` to clipboard\n7. Appears as inbox item (category: browser, dismissible)\n8. Agents resolve cross-references via GET /api/browser-snippets/\u003chash\u003e\n\n**Part of a broader cross-reference system**: Typed implicit references for prompting — `browser:\u003chash\u003e`, `image:\u003chash\u003e`, `snippet:\u003chash\u003e`, `trace:\u003chash\u003e`. Each has a storage backend, API endpoint, and agent-resolvable lookup. First instance is browser snippets.\n\n**Prior art / reference implementations**:\n- chrome-element-inspector (gblikas): MV3 element picker with Vite/TS\n- theroomjs: lightweight DOM inspection engine\n- element-source (aidenybai): maps DOM elements to source files (React, Vue, Svelte, Solid)\n- Chrome DevTools MCP (Google): bridges DevTools to AI agents\n- BrowserTools MCP (AgentDesk): extension capturing DOM/screenshots for AI\n- React Grab: DOM context capture for AI consumption\n\n**Known risks**:\n- React 19 removed _debugSource from Fiber nodes (degraded source resolution)\n- Cross-origin iframes require all_frames:true\n- Some sites may block content script injection via CSP\n- Stale selectors in SPAs (mitigated by accessibility path + component name fallback)\n\n**MVP estimate**: 2-3 weeks. Picker + context extraction + Side Panel + Mandible API + clipboard + inbox integration.","files":null}]}